WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:03.030
Hi, Mystery Recapped here.

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:10.940
Today I am going to explain the American post-apocalyptic
thriller film called “Vanishing on 7th street.”

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:12.260
Spoilers ahead!

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:18.810
Watch out and take care!

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:22.949
The movie begins in a theater where a crowd
of people is enjoying a film.

00:00:22.949 --> 00:00:27.070
The projectionist Paul is in the other room
controlling the projections.

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:30.759
He has a headlamp on to help him see through
the dark cinema hall.

00:00:30.759 --> 00:00:39.090
Paul is a massive bookworm and loves to read
while he is at work.

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:44.590
We see him read a book called the lost colony
of Roanoke in which the people of a town disappear

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:45.969
mysteriously.

00:00:45.969 --> 00:00:49.890
When he gets up to push some buttons in the
control panel, the lights go off leaving the

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:52.059
theater in complete darkness.

00:00:52.059 --> 00:00:56.550
Thankfully, Paul has his headlamp which he
uses to walk inside the theater room.

00:00:56.550 --> 00:01:02.289
But to his surprise, the place that was filled
with people some seconds ago is now completely

00:01:02.289 --> 00:01:03.289
empty.

00:01:03.289 --> 00:01:04.289
He walks out to the hallways and the lights
suddenly turn on.

00:01:04.289 --> 00:01:05.580
To Paul’s utter surprise, the hallway is
filled with people’s clothes and popcorn

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:07.110
boxes on the floor as if all of them disappeared
at once.

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:09.920
He runs down the hallway calling for his colleagues.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:13.490
A guard with a torchlight who is just as confused
hears him.

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:16.770
The two then walk around the place looking
for people.

00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:21.420
The guard notices someone in a dark corner
and approaches them, but his torchlight stops

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:22.450
working midway.

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:28.299
When Paul looks back at him, the guard is
gone and his clothes are on the floor.

00:01:28.299 --> 00:01:33.030
Somewhere else in a hospital, a nurse named
Rosemary is distraught because of a similar

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:34.030
event.

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:37.170
The place is dark and no one is around except
for her.

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:40.740
She walks down the hallway with a torchlight,
but finds no one.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:44.719
Rosemary enters the operation room and finds
a patient on the bed.

00:01:44.719 --> 00:01:48.770
His body has been cut as if the surgeons left
him mid-surgery.

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:52.720
All of a sudden, the lights of the room go
out and the patient disappears.

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:57.329
A terrified Rosemary starts looking for her
baby Manny.

00:01:57.329 --> 00:02:02.300
The next morning, a TV reporter named Luke
Ryder wakes up to see his partner hasn’t

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:03.300
returned home.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:07.490
He blows the candles on his side table which
is probably the reason he hasn’t vanished

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:08.550
like the rest.

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:12.680
Luke also notices his phone is out of battery
and the power is out.

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:16.800
Ignoring everything, he dresses up and goes
outside only to see the streets filled with

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:18.980
abandoned cars and clothes.

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:23.480
Confused, he starts looking around and witnesses
a plane crash nearby.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:27.880
Not knowing what to do, he rushes to his work
and sees the situation is similar.

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:31.970
All this time, he doesn’t notice a subtle
shadow following him.

00:02:31.970 --> 00:02:36.520
Luke discovers the power is out even at his
office and none of the phones work.

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:40.620
He then looks at a picture of him and his
girlfriend when suddenly a shadow outside

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:43.100
the room catches his attention.

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:46.730
After Luke leaves, we see darkness taking
over the picture.

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:51.710
Seventy-Two hours after the first disappearance,
Luke is in the street trying to start a car.

00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:55.200
Suddenly, a man bangs on the window, asking
for help.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:57.890
He has a lighter in his hands that has stopped
working.

00:02:57.890 --> 00:03:01.130
Luke locks the doors and lets the shadow take
over the man.

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:05.780
The poor guy disappears within seconds leaving
only his clothes behind.

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:09.840
After watching the man die, Luke continues
looking for a car that works.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:14.600
A little girl with a torchlight watches him
from nearby but he doesn’t notice her.

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:18.840
In his search, Luke finds a car with its headlights
on but it doesn’t start.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:25.970
Finally, in the next block, he comes across
a well-lit pub.

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:28.830
He quickly goes inside but sees no one around.

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:32.000
The bar also has people’s clothes lying
on the floor.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:34.830
He then pours himself some alcohol to calm
down.

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:37.460
Looking for the source of power, he reaches
the basement.

00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:41.711
It has a backup generator that lights up the
whole place but to his disappointment, it

00:03:41.711 --> 00:03:43.470
is about to run out of fuel.

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:47.570
All of a sudden, a twelve-year-old kid named
James points a rifle at him.

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:51.220
He asks Luke to put his torch down and takes
him upstairs.

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:55.720
James is afraid because Luke is a stranger
but Luke assures the kid that he will not

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:56.720
harm him.

00:03:56.720 --> 00:03:59.720
James finally puts the gun down and introduces
himself.

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:02.480
He turns out to be the son of the owner of
the pub.

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:06.430
He and his mother were the only ones left
after the very first disappearance.

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:11.420
His mother has gone to a church nearby to
ask for help and James is waiting for her.

00:04:11.420 --> 00:04:16.590
Luke decides to be honest with the kid and
says that it is still dark outside at 11 am.

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:20.769
Since the first disappearance, the sun has
been rising late and setting early.

00:04:20.769 --> 00:04:25.639
In a few days, they won’t have sunlight,
so the chances of James’s mother returning

00:04:25.639 --> 00:04:26.789
are very low.

00:04:26.789 --> 00:04:31.100
James doesn’t believe him and insists that
he will wait until she arrives.

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:36.810
Luke tries to convince James to come with
him if he wants to survive.

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:42.170
However, James stays adamant in his decision.

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:47.530
A while later, the nurse Rosemary barges into
the pub frantically searching for her child,

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:48.530
Manny.

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:52.199
She blames the other two for abducting Manny
and demands them to give him back.

00:04:52.199 --> 00:04:55.570
The lady then goes crazy and points a gun
at the two.

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:59.069
She only calms down after firing a shot at
the counter.

00:04:59.069 --> 00:05:03.069
Somewhere nearby, the projectionist Paul wanders
through the dark street.

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:07.139
He is seconds away from being engulfed in
the darkness when he reaches a well-lit bus

00:05:07.139 --> 00:05:08.919
stop and is saved.

00:05:08.919 --> 00:05:12.759
However, he is heavily injured and cannot
move anymore.

00:05:12.759 --> 00:05:16.509
Back at the pub, James calms Rosemary and
offers her some water.

00:05:16.509 --> 00:05:24.479
The woman says that she is looking for her
nine months old son Manny.

00:05:24.479 --> 00:05:29.340
The movie goes into a flashback and we see
Rosemary in the hospital, taking a smoke break.

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:33.189
Suddenly, the lights go out and the noise
of a car crash follows.

00:05:33.189 --> 00:05:37.819
She is saved because of the lighter she had
in hand.

00:05:37.819 --> 00:05:41.360
She somehow survives the night and goes to
her house the next morning.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:47.139
There, she goes up to the crib in her room,
hoping to see her baby only to find him missing.

00:05:47.139 --> 00:05:51.199
Back in the present, Rosemary brings out glow
sticks from her bag that she has been using

00:05:51.199 --> 00:05:52.280
to survive.

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:56.069
As they talk, a loud scream from outside catches
their attention.

00:05:56.069 --> 00:05:59.050
They contemplate if they should go look if
there’s a survivor.

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:03.319
Luke doesn’t want to take the risk but the
other two insist he save the person.

00:06:03.319 --> 00:06:07.639
At last, Luke goes searching and finds an
injured Paul at the bus stop.

00:06:07.639 --> 00:06:10.659
They hear whispers from the shadow that moves
closer.

00:06:10.659 --> 00:06:14.560
Luke somehow drags Paul to the pub, putting
his life at risk.

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:16.860
Rosemary helps Paul and dresses his wound.

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:21.129
A while later, he gains consciousness and
starts explaining how he got there.

00:06:21.129 --> 00:06:25.509
According to Paul, after everything went down,
he was safe because of his headlamp.

00:06:25.509 --> 00:06:29.759
But for a few minutes, it stopped working
and he was hit by someone on his head.

00:06:29.759 --> 00:06:33.009
The shadows soon took over him and brought
him to the void.

00:06:33.009 --> 00:06:36.319
They whispered in Paul’s ears, making him
beg for help.

00:06:36.319 --> 00:06:40.900
However, right then, his headlamp started
to work again and he was back in the streets.

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:45.219
Paul somehow managed to get to the bus stop
and that is where Luke found him.

00:06:45.219 --> 00:06:49.530
When asked about the person who hit him, Paul
tells them that there was no body or face;

00:06:49.530 --> 00:06:50.949
it was just a shadow.

00:06:50.949 --> 00:06:56.400
Rosemary, who is a catholic, tells them that
they are left behind as a punishment by God.

00:06:56.400 --> 00:07:00.410
Luke counters that there is no god and they
do not deserve this “punishment”.

00:07:00.410 --> 00:07:04.789
Suddenly, the lights flicker again, and they
go down to the basement to check the backup

00:07:04.789 --> 00:07:05.809
generator.

00:07:05.809 --> 00:07:10.479
As Luke fixes the generator, Paul tells them
about the book he read earlier; the lost colony

00:07:10.479 --> 00:07:11.530
of Roanoke.

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:17.389
He explains that in 1587, people from an island
colony named Roanoke mysteriously disappeared

00:07:17.389 --> 00:07:18.389
overnight.

00:07:18.389 --> 00:07:22.150
The rest of the world only found out when
a boat with supplies came by and the workers

00:07:22.150 --> 00:07:23.279
found the island empty.

00:07:23.279 --> 00:07:28.370
The people had left all their food, livestock,
and clothing as it is.

00:07:28.370 --> 00:07:33.629
The only thing they left behind was the word
Croatoan written on a metal fence.

00:07:33.629 --> 00:07:37.770
Luke inquires what the word means but Paul
claims it to be a mystery.

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:41.240
Frustrated, Paul starts kicking the generator
and injures himself.

00:07:41.240 --> 00:07:44.480
He is then brought and kept on the pool table
by the others.

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:47.470
Rosemary asks Luke to get some ice for the
injured.

00:07:47.470 --> 00:07:51.219
While getting those, Luke remembers the last
time he was at his office.

00:07:51.219 --> 00:07:54.960
He is in the broadcasting studio where he
finds the last news recording.

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:59.629
The woman reporter vanishes into thin air
while talking.

00:07:59.629 --> 00:08:03.580
Then, a live feed from Chicago broadcasts
is played.

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:07.430
A person warns everyone to keep a light with
them all the time.

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:12.979
He also claims that the darkness may take
on any shape or form to lure you to your death,

00:08:12.979 --> 00:08:16.249
hence not to trust anybody except light.

00:08:16.249 --> 00:08:19.870
Back in the present, Luke gets an idea to
get out of the situation.

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:24.080
If he somehow finds a way to get to Chicago,
they can meet the other survivors and then

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:25.389
decide what to do.

00:08:25.389 --> 00:08:29.660
He remembers the working truck he has encountered
earlier and suggests to others that they should

00:08:29.660 --> 00:08:31.090
retrieve the vehicle.

00:08:31.090 --> 00:08:35.370
Since the generator can fail at any time,
they should instead use it to ignite the vehicle

00:08:35.370 --> 00:08:37.040
and drive away from the place.

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:42.110
Rosemary is skeptical of the idea because
she believes all this is happening for a reason.

00:08:42.110 --> 00:08:44.690
But Luke persuades her to join the plan.

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:49.070
They decide that James should stay with Paul
and take care of him while Rosemary and Luke

00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:50.410
go to get the vehicle.

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:54.600
In the following scene, Rosemary and Luke
manage to get to the truck and start pushing

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:56.320
it to get it back to the pub.

00:08:56.320 --> 00:09:00.750
At the same time, Paul starts questioning
James about several things in his life.

00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:04.950
He is slowly losing consciousness but James
asks him to stay awake.

00:09:04.950 --> 00:09:08.050
He requests James to play a song that they
both enjoy.

00:09:08.050 --> 00:09:13.440
James starts imagining the bar full of people
and enjoys the fantasy amidst the chaos.

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:16.460
He is only brought back when Paul asks him
to get him some water.

00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:21.300
James goes to the sink to fetch it but suddenly
the lights flicker and go off.

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:25.110
Somewhere else, Luke and Rosemary take a break
from pushing the vehicle.

00:09:25.110 --> 00:09:27.790
Luke tells her about his ex-wife, Anna, in
Chicago.

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:32.370
As they talk, they see a little girl holding
a torchlight at a distance.

00:09:32.370 --> 00:09:36.210
It is the same girl who was watching Luke
earlier when he was on the road.

00:09:36.210 --> 00:09:39.380
They try to get closer to her but the little
girl runs away.

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:44.100
Luke goes behind her and is almost engulfed
by the shadows but he is saved at the last

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:46.160
minute because of the truck’s headlight.

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:51.310
In the following scene, Paul gets up and looks
for James only to find his clothes on the

00:09:51.310 --> 00:09:54.380
floor.

00:09:54.380 --> 00:09:58.450
He walks up to the basement and sees a door
that leads to a well-lit tunnel.

00:09:58.450 --> 00:10:02.730
He goes inside, still looking for James but
comes across a dead end.

00:10:02.730 --> 00:10:06.880
The lights start to go out on their own and
he is soon engulfed by the shadows.

00:10:06.880 --> 00:10:10.550
But then, it is shown that Paul’s clothes
are on the pool table.

00:10:10.550 --> 00:10:12.850
Him getting to the tunnel was just his dream.

00:10:12.850 --> 00:10:17.070
Paul was actually unconscious and was taken
by the shadows while he was still on the pool

00:10:17.070 --> 00:10:18.070
table.

00:10:18.070 --> 00:10:24.620
James quickly comes back to Paul and sees
that he is gone.

00:10:24.620 --> 00:10:29.010
In the meantime, Luke and Rosemary’s torch
lights start running out of batteries all

00:10:29.010 --> 00:10:30.040
at once.

00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:34.000
Luke tries to ignite the fuel to create light
but they’ve got no lighter.

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:38.120
So the two go to a nearby hospital, searching
for any source of light.

00:10:38.120 --> 00:10:41.450
There, Luke ignites a fire with a matchstick
and a cloth.

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:44.940
Rosemary goes to find rubbing alcohol which
they can use as fuel.

00:10:44.940 --> 00:10:50.540
But on her way, she hears a baby crying and
sees a stroller right under a streetlight.

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:55.310
Unknown that it is the shadow’s tactic to
lure her in, Rosemary walks up to the stroller.

00:10:55.310 --> 00:11:00.000
She notices the stroller is empty but it is
too later as she is taken by the shadows.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:04.220
Luke, who is now alone, somehow gets back
to the pub with the truck.

00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:08.730
He reunites with James and the two get in
the truck ready to leave for Chicago.

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:13.260
Luke uses the backup generator to start the
engine and the two finally drive away.

00:11:13.260 --> 00:11:17.920
However, they are soon met with an accident
that happens to be right in front of a church.

00:11:17.920 --> 00:11:20.910
James insists he has to go in to look for
his mother.

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:25.160
Despite Luke warning him to stay in the car,
James runs inside the church.

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:32.030
Just then, Luke sees the word Croatoan carved
in a road sign.

00:11:32.030 --> 00:11:36.590
He rushes back to James and saves him seconds
before the shadows get him.

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:40.300
Luke then asks the kid to return with him
but is ignored again.

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:44.960
James claims that his mother is nearby because
he heard her call him, unknown that it was

00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:46.940
just a trap set by the shadows.

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:51.310
Suddenly, the car’s headlights turn off
and Luke vanishes in thin air.

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:54.260
Now, the only survivor left is James.

00:11:54.260 --> 00:11:59.020
He sits in between the lit candles of the
church but all of them slowly extinguish.

00:11:59.020 --> 00:12:01.840
The next morning, the sun finally rises.

00:12:01.840 --> 00:12:06.690
Surprisingly, James has survived the night
and is sleeping where he was yesterday.

00:12:06.690 --> 00:12:11.230
The little girl from earlier approaches him
and introduces herself as Briana.

00:12:11.230 --> 00:12:18.000
She shows James her solar flashlight that
she has been using to survive.

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:25.130
Later, both of them come outside the church
and see a horse in the middle of the road.

00:12:25.130 --> 00:12:29.340
The two get on the horse and start their journey,
presumably to a safe place.

00:12:29.340 --> 00:12:35.370
Soon, the sun sets and we see the shadows
of Luke, Rosemary, and Paul watching over

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:36.370
the kids.

00:12:36.370 --> 00:12:40.410
The movie ends as Briana and James continue
their journey.

00:12:40.410 --> 00:12:44.760
